<Base title="Privacy — Code Generator" description="Code Generator creates QR codes, barcodes and passwords in your browser. Values are not uploaded or stored." path="/privacy">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short version: QR codes, barcodes and passwords are created on your device. We never see the values you enter or generate.</p>

    <h2>Generating codes and passwords</h2>
    <p>QR codes, barcodes and passwords are generated in your browser. Links, text, Wi-Fi network names and passwords, contact details, product numbers and anything else you enter stay on your device. They are not uploaded, logged or stored, and nothing is saved when you close the page.</p>
    <p>Password generation uses your browser’s Web Crypto secure random generator. Copy the result into a trusted password manager; this site does not save or recover passwords.</p>
    <p>Logos you add are resized and re-encoded in your browser and are never uploaded.</p>
    <p>The codes are static: the content is inside the code itself. We don’t run redirect links, so we can’t see or count scans of your codes.</p>

    <h2>Scanning and reading</h2>
    <p>The camera only starts after you tap “Scan with camera” and your browser asks for permission. Video frames are analysed on your device, are never recorded or uploaded, and the camera switches off as soon as a code is found or you leave the page. Images you upload, drop or paste are read the same way and discarded.</p>

    <h2>Batch generation</h2>
    <p>CSV files and pasted lists are read in your browser, and the ZIP file is built on your device.</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>To understand which tools are used, we may record anonymous events such as a code being generated, an SVG being downloaded or a logo being added, with the tool name and QR code type (for example “wifi”). Events never include what a code or password contains, file names or anything you typed. We don’t use cookies or advertising identifiers, and our server logs don’t store IP addresses.</p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>The site may show advertising in the future. If it does, ads will never be placed over the generator, preview, scanner or download buttons, and this page will be updated to name the provider and what it collects.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Code Generator is run by Sequence Industries.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

